From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:21:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 520/526] [DS4.1] The packed BF16 head packs with TileLang in
 vLLM; B12X's packed projection goes

The served DS4.1 head (VLLM_DS41_PACKED_BF16_LM_HEAD=1) is packed at load
by B12X's packer (spark-ds41f's B12X patch 0012), the last B12X call the
head needs: its projection is TileLang's already. The packer moves into
vLLM (vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/vocab_pack.py) with the same
format, window choice, exception order and refusal, so the packed tensors
are B12X's byte for byte:

- PackedBf16Weight, pack(weight, in_place=...), unpack and is_supported,
  B12X's contract (is_supported: SM120/SM121 with TileLang).
- Three TileLang passes for B12X's three Triton ones: the exponent
  histogram (shared-memory counts, one global add a bin and block), the
  per-row exception counts (a warp a row) and the row pack (a warp a row:
  each 128-column group as four 32-column parts in column order, a warp
  prefix sum placing a part's exceptions, every encoded value decoded and
  compared with its source bits). The window choice, the row-offset
  prefix sum, the 1,024-row staging block of the in-place pack and the
  round-trip refusal are B12X's host code unchanged.

The packed head is TileLang's only: ParallelLMHead refuses it unless the
linear backend is tilelang, the logits processor's B12X packed branches go
(B12X's packed projection existed only in that patch), and so does
vllm.utils.b12x's accessor for it. The B12X BF16 vocabulary projection of
other models stays.

Tests: the TileLang vocabulary tests pack with vLLM's packer (they skipped
without B12X before); B12X's packer tests, ported (every value class
round-trips, exceptions in column order, the window rule and its tie,
allocations, the in-place pack's one staging block, refusals); and B12X's
packed-head integration test, ported to TileLang (ParallelLMHead's method
packs in its own storage and the target and drafter processors project it,
batch-invariant, on graph replay). The B12X packed-head test goes.
